--TEST--
`Core\Csrf::token` opens the session on its first use, so it needs no started session, and with no `[http] csrf_key` it throws a `RuntimeError` naming that key — `rule:core-classes/a-session-opens-on-its-first-use`
--GET--
under=a-request
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Csrf::token
// No `Core\Session` method runs first: `token` opens the session itself.
// This case writes no `[http] csrf_key`, so `token` throws naming it.
try {
    echo Core\Csrf::token();
} catch (RuntimeError $missing) {
    echo "with no key: ", Core\Str::contains($missing->message, "[http] csrf_key") ? "names the key" : $missing->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
with no key: names the key
